From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:00:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tools/tests: a changed nso_syms.py rewrites again in the NRO
 pack test

patch_nso.py imports nso_syms.py and records its hash in build_src.sha256,
so build_ipa_from_nsp.rewrite() has it in its key on purpose. The test
changed smash_arc.py and nso_syms.py in turn and expected one rewrite in
all, so it failed with 2 != 1 on main. smash_arc.py only feeds the
collection, so it still keeps the rewrite. nso_syms.py now expects the
second one.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#3029
Reason: Tool tests fail on upstream main: the NRO pack test expects no rewrite after an nso_syms.py change
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1448
---
 dm/tools/tests/test_nro_pack.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/tools/tests/test_nro_pack.py b/dm/tools/tests/test_nro_pack.py
index bc908ab..9b0e365 100644
--- a/dm/tools/tests/test_nro_pack.py
+++ b/dm/tools/tests/test_nro_pack.py
@@ -52,9 +52,9 @@ class NroPack(unittest.TestCase):
     def test_parser_changes_recollect(self):
         self.build()
         (self.repo / 'dm/gfx/tools/smash_arc.py').write_text('v2'); self.build()
-        self.assertEqual((self.collections, self.rewrites), (2, 1))   # identical collected bytes can reuse the rewrite
+        self.assertEqual((self.collections, self.rewrites), (2, 1))   # identical collected bytes do not need another rewrite
         (self.repo / 'dm/tools/nso_syms.py').write_text('v2'); self.build()
-        self.assertEqual((self.collections, self.rewrites), (3, 2))   # the rewriter also reads symbols directly
+        self.assertEqual((self.collections, self.rewrites), (3, 2))   # patch_nso.py imports nso_syms.py, so the rewrite's own key has it too
 
     def test_removed_registration_drops_stale_manifest(self):
         self.build(); (self.rom / 'game.nrr').unlink(); self.build()
